<section><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">The Physics</p><h2>Why earth-sheltered saunas hold heat better</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p class="lead">A barrel sauna fights the weather; a cabin sauna leaks heat through every wall. A cave sauna is wrapped in earth — the best insulator there is. It heats faster, holds temperature longer, uses less wood or power, and the domed vault rolls steam around the room instead of trapping it at the ceiling.</p>
</div></section>

<section style="background:#efe9db"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">Which Sauna</p><h2>Garden sauna, outdoor sauna or underground sauna?</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom:26px">Three things get sold as an outdoor sauna in the UK. They are not the same purchase, and the differences are in heat, lifespan and what is included, not just the price.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table class="spec">
    <tr><th></th><th>Barrel or pod garden sauna</th><th>Timber cabin sauna</th><th>Underground cave sauna</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Structure</td><td>Thin timber staves, above ground</td><td>Insulated timber cabin, above ground</td><td>Precast insulated vault under a metre of earth</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Heat retention</td><td>Loses heat through every stave; slow in winter</td><td>Better, still weather-dependent</td><td>Earth-wrapped; heats faster, holds longer, uses less fuel</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Lifespan</td><td>Timber weathers; retreat every year or two</td><td>Timber maintenance ongoing</td><td>Concrete does not rot or warp; 25-year structural warranty</td></tr>
    <tr><td>What you buy</td><td>The sauna, delivered; base, power and siting are yours</td><td>Usually supply and fit of the cabin only</td><td>Turnkey: design, planning if needed, groundworks, craning, installation, services, finish</td></tr>
    <tr><td>In the garden</td><td>A wooden barrel on the lawn</td><td>A shed-sized building</td><td>A grass mound and an oak door</td></tr>
    <tr><td>From (excl. VAT)</td><td>A few thousand pounds</td><td>Varies widely</td><td>£30,000 installed</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p style="margin-top:18px;max-width:720px">If you want a sauna this year for the least outlay, a barrel sauna is the honest answer. If you want a sauna that still performs in twenty years, disappears into the garden and comes installed, the cave sauna is the only one of the three built for that. <a href="/start-your-project/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Check whether your garden and budget fit in two minutes</a>.</p>
</div></section>

