<section style="background:#efe9db"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">FAQ</p><h2>Your questions, answered</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <div class="faq-item"><h3>What is an underground sauna?</h3><p>An underground sauna is a precast, insulated vault set into the ground and covered with earth, with the stove, benches and glazed entrance inside. Luxury Modules installs Revonia cave saunas across the UK as the official turnkey partner, from 4.5m² and £30,000 excl. VAT installed, with a 25-year structural warranty.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>Wood-fired or electric?</h3><p>Both are available. Wood-burning stoves are hand-matched to the room volume; electric heaters suit sites where flues are impractical.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>Does an outdoor sauna need planning permission?</h3><p>Smaller cave saunas often fall within permitted development. Where consent is needed we handle it end to end — see the planning guide.</p></div><div class="faq-item"><h3>What maintenance does it need?</h3><p>Very little. The concrete vault does not rot, warp or need retreating like timber saunas; interior woodwork needs only the care of any quality sauna.</p></div>
  <p style="margin-top:18px;font-size:14.5px">More questions? <a href="/faq/" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">See the full FAQ</a>.</p>
